cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying article using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >-
  Simulation and maximum likelihood estimation for a stochastic
  convection-diffusion equation: Fortran spectral Galerkin implementation
abstract: >-
  Fortran implementation of a spectral Galerkin discretization of a stochastic
  convection-diffusion equation with additive noise. It simulates the modal
  SDE system with the Euler-Maruyama scheme, computes maximum likelihood
  estimators of the diffusion and convection coefficients, runs Monte Carlo
  studies, and provides scripts that reproduce the figures of the article.
